## Approach

Create a new `health/scoring.rs` module implementing category-capped scoring from `HealthFindingRow`s, using repowise-calibrated biomarker weights. Each biomarker maps to one of five health categories; each category has a deduction cap. When findings in a category exceed the cap, all deductions in that category are proportionally scaled so per-finding attribution is preserved. Then rewrite the `file_health` MCP tool to query findings from DB, score them, and return findings + derived scores instead of the old hardcoded sub-scores.

The old `compute_file_scores`/`FileScores` stay in file_health.rs since `pipeline.rs::compute_snapshot_aggregates` still imports them — sutra/91 (health snapshots) replaces that callsite.

